  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-25: "Yes let me know when done and continue with next tasks" (repeated). Issue #2632 (read it in full: gh issue view 2632) and DI-144 in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md. ebilling-r1 task 165b-3 (EB-D-208) added the one helper for this rule on master: `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/WriterCreatedRecord.cs` (`AddConditions(FilterExpression, Guid)`, `AddConditions(LinkEntity, Guid)`, `FetchXmlFilter`; refuses Guid.Empty). Its guard `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/WriterCreatedRecordSingleSourceGuardTests.cs` baselines the ontology's remaining createdby-only sites: DecisionCommitService.cs 1 (~2245, the review-id lookup), DecisionRecordWriter.cs 3 (~899, ~1205, ~1983 `AddBillingWriterFilterAsync`), SignalReadService.cs 1 (FetchXML condition), SignalReevaluationJob.cs 1 (~962). A seventh site, `GateDecisionRecordSharing.cs` (~507/~521), compares a read row's createdby in memory and is invisible to the scan. Line numbers are at origin/master 1b89025736; search by name.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, Dataverse SDK QueryExpression / FetchXML, the ontology Decision Record writer and read path.</role>
  <goal>Every one of those lookups uses WriterCreatedRecord (QueryExpression, link or FetchXML form), the in-memory gate check also requires createdonbehalfby empty, and the guard's Baseline dictionary is empty; rows the writer created (createdonbehalfby empty) are still found exactly as today.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>This is defence-in-depth, not a reachable defect: the writer never impersonates (96 of 96 dev Decision Records have createdonbehalfby empty). Keep each site's other conditions, ordering, TopCount and error handling (a writer-id fault still fails the caller closed, never reads as "no record"). For the in-memory site add createdonbehalfby to the ColumnSet and require it empty; if a shared in-memory predicate on WriterCreatedRecord is the cleanest single owner, add it there (answer the three §11 questions in the PR), otherwise keep it local with a comment citing WriterCreatedRecord. Lower the guard's Baseline entries as sites move (TheBaseline_IsTight enforces it) and remove the dictionary entries at zero; do not weaken the guard. ebilling owns WriterCreatedRecord.cs: a change to it needs their review (tell the main session). Read `git log -5` on each file and run /conflict-check (ebilling-r1 merges into Signals code).</background>
  </context>
