  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">For each lookup family (commit review-id lookup, gate record lookup, condition-cleared record lookup, billing writer filter, re-evaluation lookup, read-route FetchXML, gate sharing in-memory check) a test shows a row with the writer as createdby and a non-empty createdonbehalfby is NOT trusted; each test fails with the new condition removed (state how you proved it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must-not-fire: rows with the writer as createdby and createdonbehalfby empty are still found by every lookup; existing DecisionRecordWriter, DecisionCommit, SignalRead, SignalReevaluation and GateDecisionRecordSharing tests pass unmodified; the Signals contract baselines are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">WriterCreatedRecordSingleSourceGuardTests passes with an empty Baseline (no createdby/createdonbehalfby condition outside WriterCreatedRecord in Services/Signals or Services/Finance); build, filtered tests (Signals, WriterCreatedRecord, Finance) and full ArchTests pass; publish-size delta reported.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
